// SVG parsing into cubic bezier outlines, bound to nanosvg.
//
// nanosvg depends on `<string.h>`, `<stdlib.h>`, `<stdio.h>` and `<math.h>` and nothing else, and
// it is not a library anybody has installed, so its header is carried in this package. There is no
// `dependencies` block.
//
// This is the block a *consumer* writes to reach this package:
//
//     dependencies {
//       nanosvg { git = "github.com/sysl-lang/nanosvg", version = "0.1.2" }
//     }
//
// The module a program imports is `sh.sysl.nanosvg`; the package name is the short one.

package {
  name    = "nanosvg"
  version = "0.1.2"
  sysl    = "0.9.0"
}

// **`heap` and nothing else.** nanosvg `malloc`s an image as a tree of small blocks and
// `nsvgDelete` frees it, so a parse needs an allocator. It reads no file of ours: `nsvgParseFromFile`
// is compiled in (nanosvg has no switch for it) but nothing here calls it, and `sysl.fs` hands the
// bytes over instead -- the same reason `stb` states no `posix`.
//
// **Not buildable on a bare board.** nanosvg includes `<string.h>`, `<stdlib.h>` and `<stdio.h>`
// unconditionally, which a freestanding clang does not ship; it compiles with a libc (newlib).
// README has the two commands and their answers.
requires {
  heap = true
}

// **`m` is linked**: the parser reaches `sqrtf`, `cosf`, `tanf` and `fabsf` for arcs, rotations and
// bounds.
